hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1196","Bundar told us, Abdul Rahman, Sufyan told us, and Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb told us, Abu Khaled told us, Sufyan, H. Sallam ibn Junada, narrated to us, Waki`, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, said: He was the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He performs two rak’ahs after every prescribed prayer, except for Fajr and Asr.” This is a comprehensive hadith statement"
"1197","Mu’mal ibn Hisham and Ahmad ibn Mani’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, two rak’ahs before noon, two rak’ahs after it, two rak’ahs after sunset in his house, and two rak’ahs after Dinner at his house.” Ahmad’s hadith ended, and Ma’mal added, saying: Hafsa spoke to me, and it was a time when no one entered him. He said: “He was praying.” Two rak'ahs until dawn comes, and the caller calls for prayer.\ He said: I see it. He said: Two short rak'ahs"","" and two rak'ahs after the Friday prayer in his house."""""
"1198","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah On the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to pray two rak’ahs before noon, two rak’ahs after it, and after sunset.” Two rak'ahs, and after dinner two rak'ahs.\ Ibn Umar said: Hafsa mentioned to me: “I did not see him praying two rak’ahs when dawn came.”"""""
